[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186125074 :question/answer-fields 17592186123044] [:db/retract 17592186125078 :question/answer-fields 17592186123068] {:db/id 17592186124463 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :question/id #uuid "4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-71400" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,1,1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz))\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\text{ }i+\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j+\\frac{1}{z}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(1,1,1) & =\\frac{1}{1}\\,i+\\frac{1}{1}\\,j+\\frac{1}{1}\\,k \\\\  & =i+j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $i+j+k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326" :answer-field/id #uuid "f14cf0d4-83ef-5fb3-b242-66382b80f326" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" "answer-1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" "answer-e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" "answer-e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" :answer/id #uuid "c8f30ca4-75c7-5d71-83ef-390f43fece84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" :answer/id #uuid "1fc28fd4-0332-5dca-9124-fbc2512f4f90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer/id #uuid "47b2da7a-a030-51c5-b002-05391f108200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" :answer/id #uuid "e8e5fc00-b4cc-5045-8cb1-ac186e6219f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea" :answer/id #uuid "e2579daa-2b83-50d8-a9be-1387a386e9ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124462 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465" :question/id #uuid "28dded9d-d02a-5f94-8a43-d32ef32c8465" :question/math-academy-id "q-130720" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve ${x}^{3}{y}^{2}=2x+y.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}{y}^{2} & =2x+y \\\\ {x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-1,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-1,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2x-y)j \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2)\\,i+(2{x}^{3}y-1)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,1) & =(3(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}-2)\\,i+(2(-1)^{3}(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i-3\\,j \\\\  & =⟨1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(-1,1)=⟨1,-3⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(1,-3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-1)}{1} & =\\frac{y-1}{(-3)} \\\\ -3(x+1) & =y-1 \\\\ -3x-3 & =y-1 \\\\ 3x+y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf514b2-8d3a-5a58-a6b9-5e62c2d37fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" "answer-6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" "answer-1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" "answer-48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" :answer/id #uuid "fdd0a5cd-65c6-58a5-ac60-ab333212dddc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y+1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer/id #uuid "253ca439-cd38-5c0a-a233-00c9ea58b381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" :answer/id #uuid "6545d507-c4ab-5302-a22d-62c4ef0a3e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" :answer/id #uuid "1a0e0626-6248-5b0f-8302-6f527732a13c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c" :answer/id #uuid "48db2746-13e6-5da9-a526-f85be7161a7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-0ef48a11-b676-522a-82bb-9f39665ac76e" :activity/id #uuid "0ef48a11-b676-522a-82bb-9f39665ac76e" :activity/title "The Gradient as a Normal Vector" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050027 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91"] :activity/first-step "step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :step/id #uuid "2598a4b3-3e2b-55cf-8762-35fa24bff20e" :step/content 17592186125074 :step/next "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :step/id #uuid "628d3218-9eb5-5ad9-a24c-b47a38223247" :step/content 17592186125078 :step/next "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :step/id #uuid "7d9f5645-ab76-539c-abb6-92fcd4f5fb7f" :step/content "question-4bf356ec-77aa-55f5-9268-fd51c57a8d9c" :step/next "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :step/id #uuid "17075a61-c9d0-5adb-a8b2-23c29d75a027" :step/content 17592186403468 :step/next "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6839775f-3cbd-5361-8538-0f08a1251e91" :step/id #u